    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0462" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg366"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Beaupre.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 121.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your telegram of the 1st
                    instant, in regard to the alleged departure of a filibustering expedition from
                    the United States to Guatemala, and to the Department’s telegraphic reply of the
                    same date, confirmed in my instruction of the 3d instant, I have to inclose, for
                    your information, copies of correspondence had with the Navy Department in
                    regard to the said expedition.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>



